f=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(123.109375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(169.609375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(225.196513 62.448) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(124.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(145.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(210.3125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_17\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(283.3426 76.704) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(102.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(123.109375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(169.609375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_18\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(341.513063 116.6208) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" d=\"M 3482 4749 Q 3546 4749 3565 4729 Q 3584 4710 3578 4653 L 3552 4307 Q 3546 4262 3536 4249 Q 3526 4237 3462 4237 L 1286 4237 Q 1210 4237 1210 4166 L 1094 2778 Q 1088 2733 1113 2710 Q 1139 2688 1171 2701 Q 1408 2822 1648 2915 Q 1888 3008 2234 3008 Q 2656 3008 3021 2854 Q 3386 2701 3606 2381 Q 3827 2061 3827 1555 Q 3827 1043 3593 681 Q 3360 320 2947 128 Q 2534 -64 2003 -64 Q 1517 -64 1085 105 Q 653 275 352 602 Q 326 640 323 669 Q 320 698 365 730 L 640 954 Q 691 992 749 934 Q 922 774 1088 652 Q 1254 531 1456 464 Q 1658 397 1926 397 Q 2342 397 2630 544 Q 2918 691 3072 950 Q 3226 1210 3226 1536 Q 3226 1882 3078 2102 Q 2931 2323 2684 2432 Q 2438 2541 2138 2541 Q 1798 2541 1529 2419 Q 1261 2298 1037 2163 Q 986 2138 973 2144 Q 960 2150 922 2170 L 608 2349 Q 550 2381 553 2397 Q 557 2413 563 2490 L 736 4659 Q 742 4717 764 4733 Q 787 4749 877 4749 L 3482 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(67.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(113.90625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p20d4c5e7eb\"><rect x=\"35.299719\" y=\"9.768\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Where the $4.00 goes ($ per pack)","note":null},"answer":"<ul><li>Remove VAT: $4.00 ÷ 1.05 = $3.81</li><li>Retailer keeps 30%: $2.67 left</li> <li>Distributor keeps 15%: <b>$2.27</b> to Rill (57% of the shelf price)</li> <li>Minus $1.12 cost: <b>$1.15 contribution per pack</b></li></ul>"},{"q":"How many packs per store per week does Rill need to break even in year one and from year two? Compare with the benchmark of 20.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Year one: $270k ÷ $1.15 ÷ 120 stores ÷ 52 = <b>37.7 packs per store per week</b>.</p> <p>From year two: $110k ÷ $1.15 ÷ 120 ÷ 52 = <b>15.4</b>.</p> <p>At the benchmark of 20: year one −$0.13M, year two +$0.03M.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> expect a loss in year one, then a modest profit if Rill sells like its peers. The year-one loss takes about four more years of benchmark sales to earn back (cumulative break-even in year five), so Rill needs to beat the benchmark.</p>"},{"q":"How would you make the launch work?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Start with fewer stores</b> (the 40 best) to cut listing fees and focus sampling</li> <li><b>Negotiate listing fees</b> against volume, or pay them in instalments</li> <li><b>Sampling and eye-level shelf space</b> in the first three months: trial drives repeat</li> <li><b>Track packs per store per week</b> monthly; agree with the distributor what happens below 10</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Launch, but plan for a year-one loss. Rill keeps $2.27 of the $4.00 shelf price and earns $1.15 per pack; it needs about 38 packs per store per week to break even in year one but only about 15 after that, against a benchmark of 20. At the benchmark, it loses about $127k in year one and earns about $33k a year after. I recommend starting in the best 40 stores, focusing sampling there, and expanding once sales pass the benchmark. Risk: slow sales in year one lead retailers to delist. Next step: agree store-level targets with the distributor.","great":["Walks the price waterfall step by step, including VAT","Converts break-even into packs per store per week","Separates one-off launch costs from ongoing ones","Recommends a staged launch"],"id":40,"slug":"rill-snacks"}